   175	**Category enum (src/cma/models.py).** Six values are added and none of the existing values change. Credit categories map to buckets as follows:
   176	
   177	| Credit category | Bucket |
   178	|---|---|
   179	| revenue_card_settlement, revenue_transfer | trading receipts (M2) |
   180	| cash_deposit (new) | trading receipts (M2); also counted in cash deposits within trading receipts (M18) |
   181	| own_account_transfer (new; also used for debits) | own-account transfers in (M19) |
   182	| director_funding (new) | director and shareholder funding (M20) |
   183	| loan_drawdown | lending drawdowns (M21) |
   184	| refund_in (new), returned_dd | refunds and returned payments in (M22) |
   185	| hmrc_repayment (new) | HMRC repayments (M23) |
   186	| other_explained_in (new: grants, insurance claims, interest) | other explained money in (M24) |
   187	| other | unexplained money in (M25) |
   188	
   189	cash_deposit joins REVENUE_CATEGORIES, so M2, M3, M4, M9, M10, M28 and the monthly trading receipts include cash. M15 does not, because it reads named customer transfers only. Under v1 no line is ever categorised cash_deposit, so v1 figures do not move. In the code and the UI, `other` now means unexplained. Merchant cash advances use loan_drawdown and loan_repayment. Gambling and cash withdrawals are read by indicators, not categories. A credit in any other category is a reconciliation failure (R3).
   190	
   191	**Transaction (src/cma/models.py).** Three optional fields are added: the account key (default 'main'), the id of the rule, firm rule or override that set the category, and the provider's category as an untrusted hint. Amount and balance keep their current types where the model meets the rest of the code; the figures layer converts them to pence.
   192	
   193	**New figures.** No id is ever reused. M1-M16 keep their ids and units. M16 is renamed 'Non-trading money in (share)'; M2 keeps the name Total revenue, and its method sentence now names cash paid in. Values move only on lines a v2 rule now recognises (R10).
   194	
